---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import { site } from '../config/site.js';
---

<PageLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description={`How ${site.name} handles your data: the tools run in your browser, nothing you enter is uploaded, and the only thing saved is your theme choice.`}
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="Legal"
    title="Privacy Policy"
    intro="A plain-language description of what this website does with your information."
    crumbs={[{ label: 'Privacy Policy' }]}
  />
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="prose">
        <p class="notice">
          <strong>Draft.</strong> This page describes how the website works today. It has not been reviewed by a legal professional,
          and the operator’s contact and hosting details will be added before launch.
        </p>

        <h2>The short version</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>The tools process your files and text in your own browser. {site.name} does not receive them.</li>
          <li>There are no accounts, no advertising and no analytics or tracking scripts on this site.</li>
          <li>The only thing saved on your device is your light or dark theme choice.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>What you enter into the tools</h2>
        <p>
          Images you add to the Image Compressor and Image Resizer, text in the Word Counter, JSON in the JSON Formatter, and the details you enter in
          the WiFi QR Generator and QR Code Generator (including WiFi passwords, email addresses, phone numbers and contact details) are processed by
          your browser on your device. They are not sent to {site.name} or to any third party, are not added to the page address, and are not kept
          after you close or reload the page. Files you download are created on your device.
        </p>

        <h2>What is stored on your device</h2>
        <p>
          If you switch between the light and dark theme, your choice is saved in your browser’s local storage under the name <code>theme</code>
          so the site can remember it. It contains only the word “light” or “dark”. The site does not set cookies.
        </p>

        <h2>Information your browser sends when you visit</h2>
        <p>
          Like any website, loading a page means your browser requests it from the web server that hosts the site, and that server receives normal
          technical details such as your IP address and the page requested. The hosting provider has not been named here yet; this page will be updated
          to say who it is and how long such logs are kept. {site.name} does not add its own analytics on top of this.
        </p>

        <h2>The contact form</h2>
        <p>
          The form on the <a href="/contact">Contact</a> page is currently a placeholder. It checks what you type but does not send it anywhere.
        </p>

        <h2>Questions</h2>
        <p>See the <a href="/help">Help / FAQ</a> page or <a href="/contact">contact us</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</PageLayout>
